## 3. Contribution and Publication Guidelines

All modifications or additions to this taxonomy must adhere to the following rules to maintain consistency and quality.

*   Scope Adherence: All proposed changes must align with the existing nine threat domains. Proposals for new domains require a formal review by the AI Risk Committee.
*   Structured Submissions: All changes must be submitted via a Pull Request (PR) against the `main` branch of this repository.
*   Evidence-Based Additions: New sub-threats should be justified with references to published research, established security frameworks (e.g., MITRE ATLAS), or documented real-world incidents.
*   Concise and Technical Language: Scenario descriptions must not exceed 20 words and must maintain a technical, unambiguous tone.
*   Peer Review: All PRs require at least two approvals from designated reviewers before being merged.

